  "notes": "NY trio carrying Brian Alexander Morgan's melodic hip-hop-soul with a house/disco undertow, 1992–1997. The research gives \"63–74 half-time ballads + 85–99 straight uptempo\" and the published sheet for the signature record is D minor at 63 marked \"slow groove\", so the ballad spine is the base: 63–74, `halfTime` true, snare on beat 3. The three drum deltas are the entry's: \"a soft 2&4\" folded to the doubled grid so the kick loses the parent's and-of-4 habit, \"a snare-roll pickup into the chorus\" which is why `snareRollLadder` is on and the roll positions are pre-downbeat, and \"shaker on offbeat 8ths\" which is a dedicated offbeat perc lane rather than a hat pattern. Harmony is \"diatonic minor with i–iv–V and added-9th pads; 4-bar loops\" — encoded literally, with the ninth share above the parent's. \"Coko's soprano riding above the harmony rather than inside it — the arrangement leaves the top voice free for melisma\" is the high melody register, the low `chordToneBias` and the thin countermelody. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are `swing.amount` 0.52, every velocity/density number and the bass block; the research marks the bass's \"short slide into the downbeat\" `[LOW-CONF]`, which is carried here as a modest `glideProb` rather than a signature.",
